    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49912" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ūrīnor</span></b> ,
		āri, v. dep. (ante-class. collat.
		form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ūrīno</span></b> ,
		āre) [urina; Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐρέω</span>],
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to plunge under
				water</i>, <i>to dive</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urinare est mergi in aquam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, § 126</span></i>
			 Müll.; Cic. Fragm. ap. <i><span class="en">Non.
				474, 27</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 11, 37, 72, §
				188</span></i>.—Part.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urinantes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
				9</span></i>
			 30, 48, § 91.</div>
